    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **34 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `membershipTier` field is computed by `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto()` at response time (both the POST-create response and every GET go through this mapper), so that's where the GOLD rule belongs.\n\nI changed `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n\n- Converted the mapper from an `interface` to an `abstract class` (MapStruct is configured with `defaultComponentModel=spring`, so the generated `OwnerMapperImpl` is a Spring `@Component`), which lets it hold an `@Autowired OwnerRepository`.\n- Replaced the inline `membershipTier` expression with a call to a new `protected String membershipTier(Owner owner)` method that:\n  - Returns `GOLD` when the owner has a non-blank `householdId` and 3+ owners share that `householdId` (counted live via the repository \u2014 so it reflects state \"after this create\", including the back-filled housemates from `AssignHousehold`).\n  - Otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER (no namesakes + non-blank email) / BRONZE rules.\n\nRepository access during mapping is safe: the GET pipeline's `respond` step runs under `readonly-transaction` governance, and the POST create response runs within the write transaction after `SaveOwner`.\n\nThe new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD for a 3-member household) passes, and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) and `Cp11Tests` (household id) continue to pass.",
